509
00:32:34,513 --> 00:32:43,162
Speaker 1: And eventually, I was able to figure out that it was only happening because the monitor has two different color modes, right?

510
00:32:43,222 --> 00:32:51,010
Speaker 1: There's RGB and YPBR, you know, the other color encoding mode that can happen, right?

511
00:32:51,551 --> 00:32:59,186
Speaker 1: And basically, one is the one that televisions use, and RGB is the one that monitors use, but nothing really stops you from using the other one.

512
00:32:59,207 --> 00:33:00,930
Speaker 1: It's not like there's something wrong with it, right?

513
00:33:01,190 --> 00:33:07,800
Speaker 1: It's like if you plug your computer into a television with the HDMI cable, it's going to use the Y whatever one, with the component one.

514
00:33:08,380 --> 00:33:10,583
Speaker 1: If you plug it into a monitor, it's going to use the RGB one.

515
00:33:10,623 --> 00:33:15,230
Speaker 1: There's a negotiation that happens between the two devices, and my monitor supported both.

516
00:33:15,771 --> 00:33:17,353
Speaker 1: So why shouldn't both of them work?

517
00:33:17,593 --> 00:33:31,650
