846
00:56:48,529 --> 00:56:49,610
Speaker 0: But that pin is for power.

847
00:56:50,230 --> 00:57:01,120
Speaker 0: So if you have a DisplayPort cable like that, then the monitor is sending 500 milliamps at three point three volts over that cable at your GPU.

848
00:57:01,901 --> 00:57:07,408
Speaker 0: But your GPU is sending 500 milliamps or three point three volts at the monitor.

849
00:57:07,889 --> 00:57:16,720
Speaker 0: And what are the ramifications of this kind of random, depending on a lot of factors like there's no way to troubleshoot that shit.

